Eugene V. Debs (born November 5, 1855, Terre Haute, 
Indiana, U.S.—died October 20, 1926, 
Elmhurst, Illinois) was a 
labour organizer and 
Socialist Party candidate for 
U.S. president five times between 1900 and 1920.

