				"@type" : "Question",
				"name" : "<div>How did Eugene V. Debs become famous? <\/div><em><\/em>",
				"acceptedAnswer" : {
					"@type" : "Answer",
					"text" : "Eugene V. Debs was president of the newly established American Railway Union when it won national prominence by conducting a successful strike against the <a href=\"https:\/\/www.britannica.com\/money\/Great-Northern-Railway-Company\">Great Northern Railway Company<\/a> in April 1894. He gained greater renown when he was sentenced to six months in jail in 1895 for his role in leading the Chicago <a href=\"https:\/\/www.britannica.com\/event\/Pullman-Strike\">Pullman Palace Car Company strike<\/a>. "
				}
